Z||000012||Philphine||07-09-2001||12:04 PM||||hey qwik, looked at the spot and saw that bracket. it's almost right under where i put my lower mounting piece. i think i'll try that spot next time too. probaly look a little cleaner. thanks.<P>also if a junkyards too far away and that strut works well you can get a replacement at autozone. i took a guess at my last one but if this one has a bit less strenth (mine won't rip the lid off, but it's definitly more than whats needed) it may be a better choice.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||qwikgta||07-10-2001||09:27 PM||||Artherd....so go to the local parts store and buy one for a 84 Buick Regal.  Then put it on your car....Come on now, I did the leg work and told you what to get and how to do it.  This will save you BUCKS...It will cost you less than $15.00 and trust me it works perfect.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
